# Behavior-Oriented Actor Model laws

Agent(a) ∧ OwnsIntent(a, i) ∧ Realizes(i, b) → Governs(i, b)

Execute(action) → ∃ intent, behavior : Governs(intent, behavior) ∧ Contains(behavior, action)

Actor(r) → ∃! agent : BelongsTo(r, agent)

ActionExecution(x) → ∃! supervisor : Supervises(supervisor, x)

Actor(r1) ∧ Actor(r2) ∧ r1 ≠ r2 → ¬DirectWrite(r1, PrivateState(r2))

Observe(r1, r2) → PolicyAllows(r1, Projection(State(r2)))

InterAgentEffect(a, b) → ChoreographedByEvent(a, b) ∨ ExplicitCompensation(a, b)

Action(a) ∧ Effect(a, x) → DeclaredCapability(a, x)

CompositeBehavior(b) → ∀ a ∈ Actions(b) : PreservesInvariant(b, a)

State(r) = Fold(Apply, InitialState(r), AcceptedLocalEvents(r))

Intent(i) ∧ ExecutionInstance(i, x) → ImmutableSemanticIdentity(i, x)

InScopeInvocation(i) → Eventually(Ok(i) ∨ Healing(Error(i)) ∨ HumanHealingEscalation(i))
